---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"
import { runGuardRows, spendRows } from "../../data/docs-content"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="tokenomics">

          <p>
            Vector prices each chat from the tokens the provider reported on the assistant messages — input,
            output, reasoning, cache reads and cache writes — at the model catalog's list price. Automations and
            parallel agents are also written to a local ledger, and an automation is refused a start once your daily
            cap is spent.
          </p>
          <dl class="doc-rows">
            {spendRows.map(([term, detail]) => (<div><dt>{term}</dt><dd>{detail}</dd></div>))}
          </dl>
          <p class="note">
            Economics that learn: every session feeds measured token and cost evidence into model recommendations, so
            the ranking is built from what providers actually reported rather than from list prices. A model gets no
            recommendation until it has at least three recorded runs for that kind of task, and an unmeasured model
            never outranks one that reported a real cost.
          </p>
                  <h3>Usage and streaks</h3>
          <p>
            Settings → Usage reports what Vector recorded locally: lifetime tokens split into input, output, cache and
            reasoning, the cost recorded against them, chats completed, average tokens per chat, average time per run,
            the longest run and the peak day. It also keeps a daily streak with your current and longest run, seven
            days of activity, and your top five models by share of all-time token use.
          </p>
          <h3>The Run Guard, from desktop 1.99.108</h3>
          <p>
            From desktop 1.99.108, Vector holds runs to a live cap instead of checking only before they start. Vector
            checks spend after every model step and stops within one step of the cap for each agent running at the
            time. Dollars are the reported tokens at catalog
            list price unless the provider reported what the step cost, so discounts are not reflected. The npm CLI
            (1.99.99) and the CLI that <code>vectordev.ai/install</code> serves predate it, so the terminal UI and
            <code>vector run</code> with <code>--max-cost</code> and <code>--max-steps</code> get the Run Guard with the
            next CLI release, and Windows WSL servers, which run the 1.99.99 engine desktop 1.99.108 requires, get it
            once a later desktop release requires that CLI. From desktop 1.99.109, the limits are one overall set: they
            cover all your repositories together, and a repository cannot set its own.
          </p>
          <dl class="doc-rows">
            {runGuardRows.map(([term, detail]) => (<div><dt>{term}</dt><dd>{detail}</dd></div>))}
          </dl>
</DocsPage>
